notes: "Fixes the FAIL from cr/v2 on 2f7fa83 (21 found / 9 verified). The important finding was self-inflicted: the checker had been widened to admit run #3's own non-conforming row, in the same commit that introduced the rule, so the code disagreed with both the flow spec and DEC-15 and the gate green-lit the defect it exists to catch. Fixed by narrowing the code and correcting the artifact, never the reverse. Docs-only in the same commit: run #3 finding 28 records the incident, and the general rule ('a predicate's vocabulary is closed; loosening one is a rulebook change needing its own reasoning') lands as a base-flow principle and a DEC-15 consequence so it survives this WU. Finding counts corrected 27 -> 28 and the flow owner split 8 -> 9 in the two docs that cite them. Nits from the review also fixed: HARD_PREDICATES documents its hand-maintained ceiling and safe-failure direction, check_elements_map's header comment moved back above it (stranded when check_avoid_cited was inserted between comment and function), unanswered Vec -> count, and n/13 -> n/m in both specs since the denominator is counted off the rulebook. One review nit deliberately not taken: splitting doc.rs into modules — 1759 lines of which ~680 are tests, and the verifier itself refuted it for lack of concrete harm. Known and out of scope, unchanged: five W1-era docs in docs/work/ are red on the artifact contract, pre-existing and belonging to no open WU"
